class.description:
[TextInsertionServer] replaces placeholders such as [code]{player}[/code] or [code]{gold:number}[/code] in any text, for example in translated texts, dialogue lines and UI labels. A value for a placeholder comes from the first of these sources that has it: 1. The [code]args[/code] dictionary of the call ([String] or [StringName] keys). 2. A provider registered with [method register_provider]: a [Callable] that is called on every insertion and reads the current state of the game. 3. A value set with [method set_value]. 4. The [TextInsertionValues] resources added with [method add_values], the higher [member TextInsertionValues.priority] first. With equal priority, the resource added later wins. The resources listed in [member ProjectSettings.internationalization/text_insertion/default_values] are added on the first use of the server. [b]Syntax:[/b] [code]{name}[/code] inserts a value. [code]{name:modifier}[/code] passes the value through a modifier, and modifiers can be chained from left to right: [code]{item:t:upper}[/code]. [code]{{[/code] and [code]}}[/code] insert a literal brace. A brace that does not form a placeholder stays as written. If no source has a value, the placeholder stays in the text as written and a warning is printed once per name in debug builds (see [member ProjectSettings.internationalization/text_insertion/warn_missing_values]). [b]Built-in modifiers:[/b] - [code]t[/code]: translates the value as a key with [method TranslationServer.translate]. - [code]upper[/code], [code]lower[/code]: upper and lower case. - [code]capitalize[/code]: like [method String.capitalize]. - [code]number[/code]: groups the digits of a number by thousands with the separators of the current locale ([code]1,234,567.5[/code] in English, [code]1.234.567,5[/code] in German) and uses native digits where [method TranslationServer.format_number] knows them. Text that is not a plain decimal number stays as it is. - [code]f[/code]: inserts placeholders in the value itself, with the same arguments. Values are never expanded without [code]f[/code], and [code]f[/code] stops after 4 levels. Own modifiers are added with [method register_modifier]. [codeblocks] [gdscript] # A provider: called on every insertion, so the text always shows the current gold. TextInsertionServer.register_provider(&"gold", func(): return inventory.gold) TextInsertionServer.set_value(&"player", "Mara")
var line = TextInsertionServer.insert("Welcome back, {player}! You have {gold:number} gold.") var item = TextInsertionServer.insert("You found {item:t}.", { "item": "ITEM_SWORD" })
# Parse once, insert often. var greeting = TextInsertionServer.parse("Hello {player}, the {npc} greets you.") label.text = TextInsertionServer.insert_template(greeting, { "npc": "smith" }) [/gdscript] [csharp] // A provider: called on every insertion, so the text always shows the current gold. TextInsertionServer.RegisterProvider("gold", Callable.From(() => Inventory.Gold)); TextInsertionServer.SetValue("player", "Mara");
string line = TextInsertionServer.Insert("Welcome back, {player}! You have {gold:number} gold."); string item = TextInsertionServer.Insert("You found {item:t}.", new Godot.Collections.Dictionary { { "item", "ITEM_SWORD" } });
// Parse once, insert often. TextInsertionTemplate greeting = TextInsertionServer.Parse("Hello {player}, the {npc} greets you."); label.Text = TextInsertionServer.InsertTemplate(greeting, new Godot.Collections.Dictionary { { "npc", "smith" } }); [/csharp] [/codeblocks] [b]Note:[/b] The methods are thread-safe. Providers read the state of the game and are only called on the main thread; an insertion on another thread skips them and uses the other sources. Signals are always emitted on the main thread. [b]Note:[/b] [method insert] parses a text once and keeps up to 256 parsed texts in a cache. For texts that are inserted very often, keep the [TextInsertionTemplate] from [method parse] and use [method insert_template].
